    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing TTS Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. I'm focusing on incorporating the specific provider into the `synthesize_text.py` script. The goal now is to establish the clear dependency on this particular TTS service within the code's structure and behavior.\n\n\n**Implementing TTS Integration**\n\nI'm now in the process of creating the `synthesize_text.py` file. I'm building it with a clear focus on integrating the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech library. I'm making sure that the import for `google.cloud.texttospeech` and the core synthesis logic are both present, so the file works correctly.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860550649,
          "start": 1789860548508
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc008f9c001OpxBu1gxIKJTp9",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc008a9a001rYbQxRv85ZDAny",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ff75f0ffeyGjP17Th13116w",
      "time_created": 1789860548508,
      "time_updated": 1789860550650
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "bz6HTH6ykrecaFJL",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import texttospeech\nimport os\n\ndef synthesize_text(text, output_filename=\"output.mp3\"):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\"\"\"\n\n    # Set up Google Cloud credentials (if not already set via environment variable)\n    # os.environ[\"GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS\"] = \"path/to/your/keyfile.json\"\n\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    input_text = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(text=text)\n\n    # Select the language and SSML voice gender\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL,\n    )\n\n    # Select the type of audio file you want returned\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        input=input_text, voice=voice, audio_config=audio_config\n    )\n\n    # The response's audio_content is binary.\n    with open(output_filename, \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(response.audio_content)\n        print(f'Audio content written to file \"{output_filename}\"')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    text_to_synthesize = \"Hello, this is a test of the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech API.\"\n    synthesize_text(text_to_synthesize)\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_text.py"
          },
